3. Website :- 

10.png —
Customers can visit the Cleaning page on your website and book a cleaning service by filling in their personal details, selecting their preferred service, number of floors, rooms, area, cleaning shift, time slot, and choosing a date from the built-in calendar that only shows valid and available dates based on your configured shifts and holidays — so customers can never pick a blocked or unavailable date. Once everything is filled in, they simply click Submit Request to place their booking.

	Note: If the customer is already logged in to the website, all their personal details such as name, address, mobile number, email, city, ZIP code, state, and country are automatically filled in, so they only need to select the service, shift, time slot, and date to complete the booking.


10.1.png —
When a customer checks the Recurring Service option, additional fields appear where they can set how often the service should repeat using the Repeat Every field, choose the type as Daily, Weekly, or Monthly, and select an end date from the calendar — which again only shows valid available dates so the recurring schedule is always accurate and conflict-free.

	Note: The system automatically validates the end date based on the selected repeat interval, so customers cannot accidentally set an end date that does not make sense for their chosen schedule.


11.png — 
Once the customer clicks Submit Request and the booking is placed successfully, they are taken to a clean Thank You page confirming that their cleaning service request has been received and that the team will get back to them shortly.


