4. Backend Process:- 


12.png —
The dashboard gives you a live summary of your entire cleaning business showing total bookings, new requests, approvals, rejections, and total revenue all in one screen. Charts show how bookings are trending over time, which services are bringing in the most revenue, and which cleaning teams are performing the best. This helps you make better decisions and stay on top of your business without digging through individual records.

12.1.png —
From the Settings > Users & Companies and open any user profile. Under the Access Rights tab you can see all the roles assigned to that user across different modules. In the Other section you will find the Cleaning Service field where you can assign either Manager or Administrator role. A Manager can only see and manage the bookings assigned to them, while an Administrator has full access to all bookings across the business. This role-based control ensures that each team member only sees what is relevant to them, keeping the workflow clean and data secure.

13.png — 
The Booking Requests screen gives a complete overview of all incoming bookings with the reference number, customer name, mobile number, area, preferred date, pricing type, estimated amount, and current status shown in color-coded labels — New Request, Under Review, Approved, and Rejected — making it easy to track every booking at a glance.

14.png —
When a customer submits a booking from the website, it appears in Odoo as a New Request with a unique reference number like we have BR/00098, It automatically fetch all the details enter in the website form, along with the customer's full details, service type, number of floors, rooms, area, preferred date, shift, and time slot all captured automatically — The administrator can assign a manager directly from the booking form by selecting them in the Assigned Manager field, ready for the manager to review.

14.1.png —
 Administrator can also review the full pricing details and recurring service settings including the repeat interval and ending date — all in one place before moving the booking forward.

14.2.png —
We also support a fixed-price option, allowing prices to be adjusted based on customer requirements and negotiated according to their specific needs.  

15.png —
Once the booking is moved to Under Review, the assigned manager automatically receives an email notification with the booking reference for review. The manager can check employee or team availability but clicking cleaner availability button, assign the request accordingly. The manager can choose the specific employee or team based on the requirement. All actions and updates are automatically logged in the chatter on the right, ensuring complete visibility and making sure nothing is missed.

16.png — 
The Cleaner Availability button opens the availability checker where the date, shift, and time slot from the booking are pre-filled automatically, and automatically shows how many employees and teams are free — the Available Teams tab displays each team along with their shift and all team members assigned to them.

17.png — 
The Available Employees tab shows a full list of individual employees who are free for the selected date, shift, and time slot, along with their position and the shifts they are assigned to — making it easy to pick the right person for the job without any guesswork.

18.png —
Once the manager reviews and approves the booking, the status is automatically updated to Approved, with the approval date recorded instantly. Based on the selected recurring plan, the cleaning tasks are created automatically, and an approval email is sent to the customer to inform that their request has been approved. 

19.png —
For recurring bookings, the system automatically creates a separate task for each scheduled cleaning session so your team always knows exactly what jobs are coming and when. Each task is listed with its due date and the assigned team members so nothing falls through the cracks. Your cleaning staff can track and manage each session independently without any manual planning.

20.png — 
Each task contains all the information the cleaning team needs to complete the job efficiently, including all booking details. When an employee begins the task, they simply click the Start button to begin tracking their working time. Once the task is completed, they click Stop, and the recorded time is automatically added to the timesheet according to the standard Odoo workflow, ensuring accurate time tracking and proper service records.

21.png —
A Create Invoice button also appears at the top of the booking screen, allowing the admin to generate the customer’s invoice immediately as per the estimated price without leaving the page.

22 and 22.1.png —
Clicking Create Invoice generates a ready-to-send customer invoice with the customer details and the correct service amount already filled automatically. The admin simply reviews it and confirms it to make it official and ready for the customer. The further process of invoice is done as per the odoo standard flow.

